WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.163
Why this chapter?

2
00:00:01.163 --> 00:00:05.098
Because Google's notices are the
narrowest of the five providers,

3
00:00:05.098 --> 00:00:08.450
and the danger is an empty list
that looks like good news.

4
00:00:08.450 --> 00:00:10.225
So the goal has two halves.

5
00:00:10.225 --> 00:00:15.009
By the end you can read a project's or an
organization's Personalized Service Health

6
00:00:15.009 --> 00:00:18.199
incidents, with the viewer
role, into records the router

7
00:00:18.199 --> 00:00:21.250
and the weekly digest treat
like any other provider's.

8
00:00:21.250 --> 00:00:25.588
And you can tell the security officer
exactly what Google's notices don't cover.

9
00:00:25.588 --> 00:00:30.257
It's for developers who maintain the kit,
the project owner who owns this gate,

10
00:00:30.257 --> 00:00:33.140
and the security officer,
who records the gaps.
